[38;2;124;124;124m- $A_7$: $M = \mathbb{Z}/6$ (order 6, divisible by 3)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $A_n$ for $n \geq 8$: $M = \mathbb{Z}/2$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $A_6$ has Schur multiplier $\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}$, which has an element of [0m[38;2;124;124;124morder 3. Taking $p = 3$:[0m
