[38;2;124;124;124mWait, but I should double-check: is $A_6$ a nonabelian finite simple group? Yes,[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$A_6$ is simple (for $n \geq 5$, $A_n$ is simple), and it's nonabelian.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd $p = 3$ is an odd prime.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $S = A_6$ and $p = 3$ gives a nontrivial $H^2(S, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me also think about whether there are other examples. The Schur [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmultipliers of the sporadic groups and Lie type groups also have odd prime [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfactors in some cases. For instance:[0m
