[38;2;124;124;124mBut the simplest example is $A_6$ with $p = 3$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me also verify the universal coefficient theorem application more carefully.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThe universal coefficient theorem for group cohomology states that for a group [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$G$ and a trivial $G$-module $A$, there is a short exact sequence:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$0 \to \text{Ext}^1_{\mathbb{Z}}(H_{n-1}(G, \mathbb{Z}), A) \to H^n(G, A) \to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\text{Hom}(H_n(G, \mathbb{Z}), A) \to 0$$[0m

