[38;2;124;124;124m\gcd(6,3)\mathbb{Z} = \mathbb{Z}/3\mathbb{Z} \neq 0$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the answer is YES, such a group exists.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write up a clean proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, I want to be careful about the Schur multiplier of $A_6$. The Schur [0m
